    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense faces a polarized slate today, highlighted by a strong matchup for **Heliot Ramos** (63.06) against Roki Sasaki. Despite the SP_xERA appearing high at 5.30, the primary driver for **Heliot Ramos** is his favorable platoon split and his spot in the heart of the order, making him an anchor for today's production. **Gunnar Henderson** remains our overall strongest play at 64.87; although he faces a tough platoon disadvantage against Ryan Weathers, his leadoff status and 100% stolen base probability against a slow-delivering lefty make him an indispensable elite-category asset. We are leaning heavily into the speed element here, prioritizing **Gunnar Henderson**'s base-stealing potential even when the raw projected hit output is slightly dampened by the handedness matchup.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightly contested between **Nolan Schanuel** (51.34) and **Josh Jung** (48.40). While **Josh Jung** offers consistent contact, the optimizer favored **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s superior plate discipline and cleaner matchup profile against Joey Cantillo, whereas **Josh Jung** struggled to gain traction against the efficiency of Michael Soroka. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.39) and **Kyle Tucker** (53.52); both are elite talents, but they face SP_xERA figures below 4.00, with **Kyle Tucker** specifically hampered by a difficult 2.60 xERA from Trevor McDonald. We will monitor the lineup pending status for both, as any drop in their expected batting position would trigger a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** still sidelined on the IL, the depth provided by **Andy Pages** (47.07) and **Josh Lowe** (41.41) is critical for maintaining our category coverage, despite the risks posed by **Josh Lowe**\u2019s lower-order placement.",
